<title>SWITZERLAND: Duisenberg says Germans not loosening EMU stance.</title>
<headline>Duisenberg says Germans not loosening EMU stance.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wim Duisenberg, head of the Dutch central bank, said said Germany had not signaled a looser stance on membership criteria for the European single currency.</p>
<p>Duisenberg was responding to reporters' questions about news reports that Germany had signaled an easier stance on interpreting Maastricht rules for membership in European economic and monetary Union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;That is totally contrary to reality,&quot; he said about reports of a softer German stance.</p>
</text>
